# Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace every @YOUR_LOGIN. factory-gate fails
# until you do. Mirrors the tiers: the last matching line wins, and a pattern with
# no owner means nobody's approval is required by CODEOWNERS.
#
# This file makes GitHub ask for a review. The gate enforces T2 itself, because
# CODEOWNERS is case-sensitive and can't express "new file".
#
# 1. Default: everything needs a code owner (matches the T2 default).
*                 @YOUR_LOGIN

# 2. T0 and T1 paths from factory-tiers.json: unowned, so the App's approval counts.
/docs/reference/
/docs/evidence/
/scripts/
/src/
/skills/

# 3. T2 paths inside those folders go back to the owner. Keep these last.
/scripts/lint_*.py         @YOUR_LOGIN
/scripts/guard_*.py        @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.github/**              @YOUR_LOGIN
**/CODEOWNERS              @YOUR_LOGIN
**/CLAUDE.md               @YOUR_LOGIN
**/AGENTS.md               @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.claude/hooks/**        @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.claude/settings*.json  @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.claude/agents/**       @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.gitignore              @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.gitleaksignore         @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.gitattributes          @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.env*                   @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.mcp.json               @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.husky/**               @YOUR_LOGIN
**/.githooks/**            @YOUR_LOGIN
